  clock: 2  # c7b9
  nonce: c7b9  # c7b9
  message: "THE GRAMMAR IS NOT A BLOCKER -- checked 2026-09-10, on the way to shipping the\nsibling item WI-kigub (PR #908).\n\nThe arc file records both elixir cells as \"(grammar NOT installed locally)\".\nThat was never re-executed. `tree_sitter_elixir` is indeed absent from the\nvenv, but `ElixirAnalyzer` sets `language_pack_name = \"elixir\"` and\n`tree_sitter_language_pack.get_language(\"elixir\")` resolves. `analyze_elixir`\nruns on the 291-file phoenix-framework corpus and produced 2,983 symbols and\n11,100 edges in the baseline arm. THIS ITEM IS ACTIONABLE NOW.\n\nTwo things the WI-kigub work establishes that this item needs:\n\n1. MEASURE WITH `PYTHONHASHSEED=0` ON EVERY ARM. The analyzer is\n   non-deterministic across processes (WI-jozap): identical runs over the same\n   repository disagree by 67-166 edges. An unseeded A/B on this item -- which\n   REMOVES false edges as well as adding true ones, and so has a real\n   two-directional signal to read -- would be unreadable.\n\n2. THE SUBSTRING GUARD IS STILL THE ONLY GATE ON THAT PATH. WI-kigub routed\n   atom calls AROUND it rather than through it, precisely because `\"ets.\"` is\n   a substring of a project key like `Foo.Sockets.insert`; a test pins that.\n   So this item's `any(module_dot in k for k in global_symbols)` is untouched\n   and its `Logger.error -> changeset_json.ex` / `Logger.info -> defp` findings\n   should still reproduce exactly as filed.\n\nBaseline artifacts for phoenix (seeded, both arms) are reusable from\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kigub_09102026/, as are the diff/attribution\ninstruments (diff_arms.py, attribute_gap.py, compare_chains.py)."  # c7b9
