- op: discuss  # ff7a
  at: '2026-09-11T04:03:28Z'  # ff7a
  by: agent  # ff7a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ff7a
  clock: 5  # ff7a
  nonce: ff7a  # ff7a
  message: "DONE in PR (merged; see pr_ref). Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kafor_09102026/\n(PLAN.md pre-registered before any outcome number; Addendum A appended).\n\nTHIS ITEM'S FILED REPRO, RE-RUN. Both named cases reproduce on the current\ntree and both are fixed:\n  `Logger.error` -> `priv/templates/phx.gen.json/changeset_json.ex:10-14:error`\n      FILED 10 sites; there are **14, across TWO template files** (the second\n      is `installer/templates/phx_web/components/core_components.ex`).\n  `Logger.info`  -> `Phoenix.Endpoint.Cowboy2Adapter.info` (a **defp**)\n      FILED 3 sites; 4 edges.\nBoth now emit `elixir:Logger:0-0:<fn>:unresolved` and reach the Logger\ncatalogue rows.\n\nTHE FILED MECHANISM IS ONE OF TWO, and the second is why this item's implied\nfix (make the substring test a component test) would NOT have worked.\nInstrumented on the live phoenix run:\n  SUFFIX ARTIFACT  `Logger.` inside `Phoenix.Logger.install`; `Path.` inside\n                   `...StaticPath.path`; `Supervisor.` inside\n                   `Phoenix.Endpoint.Supervisor.init`. A component test rejects\n                   these.\n  NAMESPACE PREFIX `Mix.` matches `Mix.Tasks.Local.Phx` at a real component\n                   boundary. phoenix defines 56 modules under `Mix.`, and\n                   `Mix.raise/1` is still Elixir's. A component test PASSES it.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED IS NOT WHAT I PRE-REGISTERED. I built and measured the exact\nmodule-ownership gate first. It is necessary and NOT sufficient: with the gate\nexact, every edge the bare-name lookup still produced corpus-wide was still\nwrong. So the BARE-NAME RESOLUTION FOR A QUALIFIED CALL IS REMOVED, and the\nownership helper I had just written was deleted as dead code. A qualified call\nresolves by EXACT name only -- `Module.func`, or through alias expansion.\n\nTWO PREREQUISITES the old substring test had been covering for, each of which\nLOST TRUE EDGES the moment it stopped:\n  * `alias Phx.New.{Project}` -- the MULTI-ALIAS BRACE FORM -- registered NO\n    hint at all. 71 true first-party edges depended on the old accident.\n  * An alias binds its FIRST COMPONENT: `alias Mix.Tasks.Phx.Gen` makes\n    `Gen.Context.build(...)` mean `Mix.Tasks.Phx.Gen.Context.build/2`. 29 more.\nThe pre-registered control is what caught both: the first pass lost 300\nfirst-party edges, 29 of them real.\n\nMEASURED (phoenix-framework, PYTHONHASHSEED=0, both arms self-reproducing):\n  208 edges REDIRECTED, total unchanged at 11,222, symbols unchanged.\n  All 206 lost first-party edges ADJUDICATED -- 200 because the expanded module\n  is not a project module; 6 read against source and all corrections\n  (`Project.new`, `Context.new` now bind to the RIGHT first-party targets where\n  both previously hit a template's `new/2`). **REAL LOSSES: 0.**\n  io-boundaries 277 -> 293; primitives 65 -> 68, **0 lost**; `logging` 53 -> 64;\n  `process_send` 0 -> 5, a boundary KIND phoenix had never reached.\n  verify-claims: host-secret-no-logging ev=5 -> ev=7, every other verdict\n  byte-identical, **both new findings read back against source and correct**.\n\nMEASURED AT L4 as this item required (\"moves the taint walk in both directions\nand must be measured on findings at L4, not on edge counts at L2\").\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT WAS WRONG IN THE FLATTERING DIRECTION. My first adjudicator\ncompared written module text against project module names, did not model\naliases, and certified \"229/229 correctly refused\" -- hiding 29 genuine losses.\nRewritten to IMPORT the shipped `_extract_alias_hints` / `_expand_alias`."  # ff7a
